  "catalog_course_description": "It is an introductory course on commutative algebra, based on the book of M. F. Atiyah and I. G. Macdonald, titled “Introduction to commutative algebra”. This course aims to cover the following topics. 1. Rings and ideals 2. Rings and Modules of fractions 3. Primary decomposition 4. Integral Dependence and valuations 5. Noether Normalization 6. Chain conditions 7. Noetherian and Artinian rings 8. The Nullstellensatz and Spec of a ring 9. Zariski topology on Spec of a ring 10. Graded rings and modules 11. Dimension theory",
